1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
The company behind Claude just did
something OpenAI couldn't.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,200
It filed to go public — at a nine hundred
sixty-five billion dollar valuation.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:14,000
And for the first time ever, in this race,
OpenAI is the one playing catch-up.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,200
Here's exactly what happened, and why the number
on the screen flipped the entire AI industry.

5
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:24,800
Let's start with the facts, because
the headlines are getting this slightly wrong.

6
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:31,200
On June first, Anthropic confidentially
submitted a draft Form S-1 to the SEC.

7
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:36,000
In plain English: it filed the paperwork to go public.
That's the first real step toward an IPO.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,200
But notice the word "confidential."
Anthropic is not publicly traded yet.

9
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:46,800
There's no ticker. No share price. The number
of shares and the offer price aren't set.

10
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:51,600
All of that depends on SEC review and the market.

11
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:58,000
So the right way to say it: Anthropic has filed to
go public. The IPO itself is proposed — not done.

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:03,200
Now, the number everyone's screenshotting.
Nine hundred sixty-five billion dollars.

13
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:09,600
Here's where it comes from. Anthropic recently
raised sixty-five billion dollars in fresh funding.

14
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:15,200
That round valued the company at
roughly nine hundred sixty-five billion.

15
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:21,600
And one important detail — that's a private
valuation, set by investors in a funding round.

16
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:27,200
It is not the price Anthropic will IPO at.
Those are two different numbers.

17
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:32,000
But here's why it still matters so much.

18
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:37,600
That valuation, around its Series H
back in May, leapfrogged OpenAI.

19
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:44,800
OpenAI was valued at eight hundred fifty-two billion
dollars in March, after its own record raise.

20
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:51,600
So for the first time, in the private market, the maker
of Claude is worth more than the maker of ChatGPT.

21
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:57,200
So why are investors throwing this kind of money around?
It comes down to growth.

22
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:02,800
And these numbers are eye-popping. Now, fair warning:
what I'm about to say is guidance Anthropic gave investors.

23
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:07,200
It's not audited financials.

24
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:14,000
With that flag up — Anthropic told investors it expects around
ten point nine billion dollars in revenue in the second quarter.

25
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,800
That's more than double the quarter before.

26
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:24,400
It also pointed to an annualized run rate
passing fifty billion dollars.

27
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:29,600
And it says it's on pace
for its first profitable quarter.

28
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:34,800
If even most of that holds up,
it explains the valuation.

29
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:39,600
This isn't a company burning cash with no plan.

30
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:45,600
The story they're selling is rare in AI —
explosive growth that's actually turning a profit.

31
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:51,200
And this isn't just financial engineering.
There's a real product behind it.

32
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:56,800
On May twenty-eighth, Anthropic released Claude Opus 4.8.

33
00:02:56,800 --> 00:03:02,400
And it leads on the coding benchmarks
that developers actually care about.

34
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:09,200
On SWE-bench Verified — a test of fixing real
software bugs — it scored eighty-eight point six percent.

35
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:13,600
That's near the top of the industry.

36
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:18,800
Why does that matter for an IPO?
Because coding is where the money is.

37
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:24,000
Companies are paying for Claude
to write and fix their software.

38
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:29,600
So when you hear about a Claude demand
surge in the IPO coverage, that's the engine.

39
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:35,200
A model that's genuinely good at
the work businesses will pay for.

40
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:40,800
So where does this leave OpenAI?
Playing defense — for once.

41
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:46,400
OpenAI is reportedly preparing
its own confidential IPO filing.

42
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:53,200
The reporting says it's targeting a public debut in the
fall — roughly the fourth quarter of this year.

43
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:59,600
And according to that coverage, OpenAI is worried about
exactly this: getting beaten to the market by Anthropic.

44
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:05,600
Keep in mind, that timing is reported and
targeted — not confirmed by OpenAI.

45
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:11,200
But think about the symbolism.
For years, OpenAI set the pace.

46
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:16,000
ChatGPT was the moment AI went mainstream.

47
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:22,400
Now its biggest rival filed first, at a
higher valuation, with a profit story.

48
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:27,600
In a race this public,
being second to file is not a great look.

49
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:33,200
And zoom out, because this
is bigger than two companies.

50
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:38,800
Twenty twenty-six is shaping up to be the
year AI hits the public markets.

51
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:45,600
Put Anthropic, OpenAI, and Elon Musk's SpaceX together,
and you're looking at an estimated three trillion dollars

52
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:50,400
in enterprise value lining up
to enter the markets. Three trillion.

53
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:55,200
That's a wave of capital,
and a wave of scrutiny.

54
00:04:55,200 --> 00:05:01,600
Because once you're public, you answer
to shareholders every single quarter.

55
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:07,200
The hype has to become real
numbers, on a schedule.

56
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:12,800
So Anthropic filing first isn't just a flex.

57
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:19,200
It's the starting gun on the era where AI companies
have to show their math — out loud, in public.

58
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:24,800
Quick thing before the wrap-up. I'm tracking
both these filings as they move —

59
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:29,600
the prices, the dates, all of it.

60
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:36,000
If you want the plain-English version when the
real numbers drop, hit subscribe so you don't miss it.

61
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:42,400
And I'm curious: would you actually
buy Anthropic stock at this valuation?

62
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:47,200
Tell me yes or no in the comments — I read them.

63
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:52,000
Anthropic filed first. The race just flipped.

64
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:58,400
Next up — I'll break down what OpenAI's filing might
actually look like, and whether it can win the market back.

65
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:02,400
See you in that one.
